ssion generator to use these adapted weights. This addresses DeBERTa's poor calibration and static ensemble weights, as successful historical experiments showed log-loss-based checkpointing directly improves ensemble performance.", "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "Augment training data for XGBoost by adding character-level TF-IDF features from a random 10% sample of test set texts. Before extracting n-gram features (char_vectorizer_short, med, long), sample 10% of test set indices, include their texts in the training corpus for TF-IDF fitting, and extract features for all training and test texts from the same vectorizer. Keep the same training/validation split for XGBoost training. This semi-supervised approach helps XGBoost adapt to test-domain patterns without overfitting, as per the initial plan's Change #2 and successful historical experiments. Integration: modify the n-gram extraction section by first taking a random 10% sample (e.g., 195 samples) from test_df['text'] and concatenating with X_train_texts before fitting char_vectorizers. Do not modify other feature engineering steps."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
